1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,828
Here's one word, and it shows up in two files, in eight places.

2
00:00:04,728 --> 00:00:08,518
Until now, you've only ever written in one of these files.

3
00:00:09,418 --> 00:00:13,348
So today you'll find out what the other one is doing with your words,

4
00:00:13,798 --> 00:00:16,831
and you'll put two words of your own into both.

5
00:00:18,631 --> 00:00:20,902
Your fact sheet says what the story is,

6
00:00:21,352 --> 00:00:25,629
and this other file, story.mast, is what makes it happen.

7
00:00:26,529 --> 00:00:29,834
And there are five lines in your fact sheet that lean on it.

8
00:00:31,634 --> 00:00:33,988
Here's what two of them put in front of the crew.

9
00:00:34,888 --> 00:00:38,053
This is the Science console, with the hulk selected,

10
00:00:38,503 --> 00:00:43,047
and this is its Intel tab, with the sentence I wrote in Lecture 5.

11
00:00:43,947 --> 00:00:47,499
And this is the Quest Log, where Find the Derelict shows Done

12
00:00:47,949 --> 00:00:49,643
once the ship reaches the hulk.

13
00:00:51,443 --> 00:00:53,517
Scan of derelict is a promise

14
00:00:53,967 --> 00:00:56,805
that something in the game wears the word derelict.

15
00:00:57,705 --> 00:01:00,483
That's called a role, which is really just a name tag.

16
00:01:02,283 --> 00:01:06,310
Done when, signal derelict_found, is a promise too:

17
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:11,462
that the story will say derelict_found, out loud, at some moment.

18
00:01:12,362 --> 00:01:14,283
And that's called a signal.

19
00:01:16,083 --> 00:01:18,468
If the other file doesn't keep those promises,

20
00:01:18,918 --> 00:01:21,525
that Intel tab never shows my sentence,

21
00:01:21,975 --> 00:01:25,131
and that step in the Quest Log never shows Done.

22
00:01:26,931 --> 00:01:30,172
So this is story.mast,

23
00:01:30,622 --> 00:01:32,532
and you're not going to learn to read it today.

24
00:01:33,432 --> 00:01:35,662
You only need three rules.

25
00:01:36,562 --> 00:01:40,455
Change only what's between quote marks, or in a note.

26
00:01:41,355 --> 00:01:43,675
Never delete a quote mark, and never add one.

27
00:01:44,575 --> 00:01:46,587
And leave every comma right where it is.

28
00:01:48,387 --> 00:01:51,762
One more thing: a note in this file starts with a hash,

29
00:01:52,212 --> 00:01:55,492
whereas in your fact sheet it starts with two slashes.

30
00:01:57,292 --> 00:02:00,718
Control, shift, F searches the whole folder.

31
00:02:01,618 --> 00:02:04,595
I turn on match case, and match whole word,

32
00:02:05,045 --> 00:02:09,734
so that I get the role itself, and not every word that happens to have it inside.

33
00:02:10,634 --> 00:02:12,582
That gives me eight results.

34
00:02:14,382 --> 00:02:16,587
Three of them are my Scan of lines.

35
00:02:17,487 --> 00:02:19,892
The other five are in the story file,

36
00:02:20,342 --> 00:02:23,409
and three of those start with a hash, so they're notes.

37
00:02:24,309 --> 00:02:27,206
That leaves just two lines that do any work.

38
00:02:29,006 --> 00:02:30,626
Here's the hulk on Helm's map,

39
00:02:31,076 --> 00:02:34,898
and Unknown Hulk is the name the crew reads beside it.

40
00:02:35,798 --> 00:02:40,752
Science shows the same name at the top of its read-out, once the hulk is scanned.

41
00:02:41,652 --> 00:02:43,848
That name comes from this first line,

42
00:02:44,298 --> 00:02:45,845
which puts the hulk in the game.

43
00:02:46,745 --> 00:02:48,882
It has four pieces in quotes:

44
00:02:49,332 --> 00:02:51,047
its name, then a list,

45
00:02:51,497 --> 00:02:54,562
then the model, and then how it behaves.

46
00:02:55,462 --> 00:02:57,428
The list is the part that's ours.

47
00:02:58,328 --> 00:03:00,537
Its first word is the side,

48
00:03:00,987 --> 00:03:03,755
and every word after that is a role.

49
00:03:04,655 --> 00:03:07,970
So the hulk is on our side, and it wears derelict,

50
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:10,150
which means that promise is kept.

51
00:03:11,950 --> 00:03:13,768
And here's the word a second time,

52
00:03:14,218 --> 00:03:18,418
in a line that asks: when Science scans something, does it wear derelict?

53
00:03:20,218 --> 00:03:22,264
This search gives me four results.

54
00:03:23,164 --> 00:03:25,219
One is in my fact sheet,

55
00:03:25,669 --> 00:03:27,130
two are in a note,

56
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:29,756
and one is a working line.

57
00:03:31,556 --> 00:03:34,078
That line has three pieces in quotes,

58
00:03:34,528 --> 00:03:36,581
and only the last one is mine.

59
00:03:37,481 --> 00:03:41,654
The first two, quest signal and signal name, are fixed:

60
00:03:42,104 --> 00:03:44,793
touch either of them, and no quest hears anything.

61
00:03:45,693 --> 00:03:48,566
The lines above it decide when the signal is said,

62
00:03:49,016 --> 00:03:52,402
which is when a ship comes within two thousand of the hulk.

63
00:03:52,852 --> 00:03:54,026
I don't need to read those.

64
00:03:55,826 --> 00:03:58,104
The second signal is said down here,

65
00:03:58,554 --> 00:04:00,678
straight under the question about the role.

66
00:04:02,478 --> 00:04:03,396
And one more thing:

67
00:04:03,846 --> 00:04:05,360
a signal is said once,

68
00:04:05,810 --> 00:04:08,808
so a step that hasn't started yet has missed it.

69
00:04:10,608 --> 00:04:14,191
In my story, this hulk is a ghost ship.

70
00:04:15,091 --> 00:04:17,963
And I'm going to do this in the wrong order, on purpose.

71
00:04:18,863 --> 00:04:22,645
First I point my reading at a role that nobody wears.

72
00:04:23,545 --> 00:04:25,650
Lint has read both files,

73
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:30,118
and it tells me nothing in this mission wears a role called ghost_ship.

74
00:04:31,018 --> 00:04:32,227
If I played it now,

75
00:04:32,677 --> 00:04:35,779
this Intel tab on Science would simply not be there,

76
00:04:36,229 --> 00:04:37,806
and my sentence would be gone with it.

77
00:04:39,606 --> 00:04:42,152
So now I keep the promise, on line sixty-eight.

78
00:04:43,052 --> 00:04:45,108
I click just before the closing quote,

79
00:04:45,558 --> 00:04:49,452
and I type a comma, a space, and the word, and nothing else.

80
00:04:50,352 --> 00:04:53,516
And it's clean, and the hulk wears two roles now.

81
00:04:55,316 --> 00:04:59,285
There are four rules for a role, and they're on the page:

82
00:04:59,735 --> 00:05:01,972
small letters and underscores,

83
00:05:02,422 --> 00:05:04,713
the same spelling in both files,

84
00:05:05,163 --> 00:05:06,647
one thing and not many,

85
00:05:07,097 --> 00:05:09,825
and in a list your word goes last,

86
00:05:10,275 --> 00:05:13,197
because the first word is the side.

87
00:05:14,997 --> 00:05:17,256
Now the same again, with the signal.

88
00:05:18,156 --> 00:05:21,156
My step now waits for ghost_ship_found.

89
00:05:22,056 --> 00:05:24,949
And lint tells me that Find waits for that signal,

90
00:05:25,399 --> 00:05:27,070
and nothing in the mission sends it,

91
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:29,623
so the wait never ends.

92
00:05:31,423 --> 00:05:33,134
So I search for the old word,

93
00:05:33,584 --> 00:05:36,210
and there are three left, all in the story file.

94
00:05:37,110 --> 00:05:38,760
I do the working line first,

95
00:05:39,210 --> 00:05:43,119
changing the last word in quotes, and only that one.

96
00:05:44,019 --> 00:05:45,249
And now it's clean.

97
00:05:47,049 --> 00:05:49,956
Then I change the note, so that the note stays true,

98
00:05:50,406 --> 00:05:53,529
because lint doesn't read a note, and neither does the game.

99
00:05:55,329 --> 00:05:57,187
And now I count.

100
00:05:58,087 --> 00:05:59,777
The old word gives me nothing,

101
00:06:00,227 --> 00:06:03,254
and the new word gives me four.

102
00:06:05,054 --> 00:06:08,687
Remember that counting, because in two minutes you'll see why it matters.

103
00:06:10,487 --> 00:06:13,792
By now I know every word these two files share,

104
00:06:14,242 --> 00:06:16,167
so I write them down where I'll see them.

105
00:06:17,067 --> 00:06:19,664
That's two roles and two signals,

106
00:06:20,114 --> 00:06:21,854
and where each one comes from.

107
00:06:22,754 --> 00:06:25,009
Every line starts with two slashes,

108
00:06:25,459 --> 00:06:28,478
so the game skips them, and this list is just for me.

109
00:06:30,278 --> 00:06:31,956
When there are thirty of these words,

110
00:06:32,406 --> 00:06:35,982
it's how I'll spell the thirty-first the same way twice.

111
00:06:37,782 --> 00:06:38,875
Now for the honest part.

112
00:06:39,775 --> 00:06:43,468
First, a signal: I misspell it on the working line,

113
00:06:43,918 --> 00:06:46,938
and lint catches it, even though my fact sheet is fine.

114
00:06:47,838 --> 00:06:50,055
That's because for a signal,

115
00:06:50,505 --> 00:06:53,167
lint looks for the line of the story that sends it.

116
00:06:54,967 --> 00:06:58,908
Now a role: I misspell derelict in the hulk's list,

117
00:06:59,358 --> 00:07:01,150
and lint says clean.

118
00:07:02,050 --> 00:07:03,359
And here's why that is.

119
00:07:04,259 --> 00:07:10,121
For a role, lint only looks for the word between quote marks, somewhere in this file,

120
00:07:10,571 --> 00:07:14,925
and it found derelict down here, on line one hundred and three.

121
00:07:15,825 --> 00:07:19,074
It doesn't ask whether the word is in a list of roles.

122
00:07:20,874 --> 00:07:23,946
On Science, the hulk has lost its readings:

123
00:07:24,396 --> 00:07:25,849
its Mat tab is gone,

124
00:07:26,299 --> 00:07:29,821
and its Scan button just keeps saying Queue Scan.

125
00:07:30,721 --> 00:07:37,022
And in the Quest Log, Study the Derelict never shows Done, and nothing says so.

126
00:07:38,822 --> 00:07:40,596
The count does catch this one:

127
00:07:41,046 --> 00:07:43,414
I get eight, and I wanted nine.

128
00:07:44,314 --> 00:07:45,754
The page lists the rest,

129
00:07:46,204 --> 00:07:50,873
and the two to learn are that your role goes last in the list,

130
00:07:51,323 --> 00:07:53,326
and that it goes after a comma.

131
00:07:55,126 --> 00:07:57,653
The crew never sees a role or a signal.

132
00:07:58,103 --> 00:08:00,273
They only see what those words connect.

133
00:08:01,173 --> 00:08:05,681
So, here in the Quest Log, Find the Derelict is done,

134
00:08:06,131 --> 00:08:07,352
and that was my signal:

135
00:08:07,802 --> 00:08:11,647
the story said ghost_ship_found, and my step was waiting for it.

136
00:08:12,547 --> 00:08:15,226
The sensors scan the hulk by themselves,

137
00:08:15,676 --> 00:08:18,341
so the second step finishes too.

138
00:08:20,141 --> 00:08:22,751
Then on Science, I pick the hulk from the list.

139
00:08:23,651 --> 00:08:27,433
Its tab buttons are down here on the left, under its name:

140
00:08:27,883 --> 00:08:30,921
there's Scan, then Intel, and then Mat.

141
00:08:31,821 --> 00:08:35,142
I press Intel, and there's my sentence in the read-out,

142
00:08:35,592 --> 00:08:37,446
hanging on the role I gave it.

143
00:08:38,346 --> 00:08:39,987
And both logs are empty.

144
00:08:41,787 --> 00:08:43,660
Now it's time for your own words.

145
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:45,984
Give the station a role,

146
00:08:46,434 --> 00:08:49,067
and a sentence for its Mat tab on Science.

147
00:08:49,967 --> 00:08:53,102
Then rename the second signal, in both files,

148
00:08:53,552 --> 00:08:55,141
and add both to your list.

149
00:08:56,041 --> 00:08:59,178
When you play, select DS 1 on Science,

150
00:08:59,628 --> 00:09:01,866
and your sentence is in its Mat tab.

151
00:09:03,666 --> 00:09:05,730
Next time it's your first quest:

152
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:07,495
a line that names a role,

153
00:09:07,945 --> 00:09:10,644
and the game does the watching itself.
